        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0789" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg705"/>

                <head>No. 323.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee
                        to Mr. Brigham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 46.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 45, relative
                    to the imprisonment of Mr. A. K. Cutting, I have to inform you that the
                    Department recognize with much satisfaction the justice of your action and the
                    ability you have shown in your report to us of the case.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ALVEY A. ADEE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
